        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 3f6fc46dd5f94ef654b685b11fbb64f0700bb78e8da3dba9fcb55525915202d0\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: 07e6da46b9ea7945fdd6893f0d792b6231d2f6085ce90c316e086dea80b55194\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the Cisco switch to protect against known types of DoS attacks on the route processor. \n\nStep 1: Configure the default policer rates for all control plane CPU queues and save the configuration.\n\nDevice\u003e enable\nDevice# configure terminal\nDevice(config)# cpp system-default\nDefaulting CPP : Policer rate for all classes will be set to their defaults\nDevice(config)# end\nDevice# copy running-configuration startup-configuration\n\nStep 2: View the policy map and verify the correct policer rates are set according to organization-defined standards.\n\nshow policy-map control-plane\n\nStep 3: Change any policer rates to match the organization-defined standards.\n\nNote: Starting from Cisco IOS XE Fuji 16.8.1a, the creation of user-defined class-maps is not supported. A user can only enable/disable a CPU queue or change the policer rate of a CPU queue.",
          "group_id": "V-220995",
          "group_id_src": "V-220995",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000362-RTR-000110",
          "rule_id": "SV-220995r1107540_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220995r1107540_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must be configured to protect against or limit the effects of denial-of-service (DoS) attacks by employing control plane protection.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-RT-000120",
          "severity": "high",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "63f500d6-a4d8-5b82-aeb3-ef528fae1511",
          "uuid": "50a3862e-ae5c-5671-8612-16759fd2939f",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 3f6fc46dd5f94ef654b685b11fbb64f0700bb78e8da3dba9fcb55525915202d0\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: 07e6da46b9ea7945fdd6893f0d792b6231d2f6085ce90c316e086dea80b55194\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Disable gratuitous ARP as shown in the example below:\n\nSW1(config)#no ip gratuitous-arps",
